R. With the shortened forms of speech written out (do not for don't, and so on; crude: 'd is always would)
   as printed: 23.74, 22.37, 21.98 (first less last 1.76);  written out: 23.83, 22.81, 22.68 (first less last 1.15): 34% of the gap is the shortened forms
   written out, the lowest of the first six is Jane Eyre at 22.76%, and 3 of the last six are above it: Syndrome 22.97, Makers 22.99, Little Brother 22.99

S. Why the Bible saves most: cells saved in 100,000 words, the Bible less the first six novels
   in all +11850; of that: the +10154; and +7353; shall +4608; th +2589; the religious shortforms +299; lord, children, father +3897

T. The translator uses the sign for "in" after a dash, where the rulebook spells it (the referee's finding). How often can that arise?
   era 1: the word "in" 1645 times in 100,000 words
   era 2: the word "in" 1560 times in 100,000 words
   era 3: the word "in" 1344 times in 100,000 words
   (how many of those follow a dash is counted in dash.out, from the texts)

